Notebook[{
Cell["ArrayGraphics3D", "ObjectName",ExpressionUUID->"03260e33-1db1-b949-a294-8565ecf7935f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"ArrayGraphics3D", "[", "arr", "]"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"34ae8674-8e11-3648-912d-64cbe799e55b"],
 " ",
 "draws the array arr as cubes arranged in space."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"d71d0704-a88f-4948-95fa-bb9c271ddac9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"ArrayGraphics3D", "[", 
    RowBox[{"arr", ",", " ", "opts"}], "]"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"cb109af9-dcee-d540-b2e0-bd6a0c3c376a"],
 " ",
 "draws it with the given options."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"3e38cfb2-f779-4f4c-be55-9c947ef5ff6c"],

Cell["Details and Options", "NotesSection",ExpressionUUID->"4e5f2ae5-68ad-6740-9f32-563a5780bac3"],

Cell["\<\
An array of order one is drawn as a line of cubes, one of order two as a \
plane of them, and one of order three as a lattice. The entry at index tuple \
(i, j, k) sits at the point {i, j, k}, an index the array does not have \
standing at one.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"b821548f-392d-0f43-814a-426b15bd6d49"],

Cell["\<\
An array of higher order is drawn by tiling: the inner block of indices is \
drawn as a lattice, and the outer block repeats that lattice through space, \
shifted by its own extent and a gap. Everything ends up in one picture, since \
space has no room for pictures inset into pictures.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"c2d9a506-a6c3-9749-8cca-7bfce267a1ae"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The result is always a three-dimensional ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Graphics3D", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "c06cfdce-cbde-ce46-bfef-83591184b634"],
 ". For plane pictures at every order see ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["ArrayGraphics", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "951c7514-c10d-c947-9146-008efcbd007e"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"71459b6f-155e-9c48-b075-d3a032d27e0e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"\"\<Nesting\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"k1", ",", " ", "k2", ",", " ", "..."}], "}"}]}], "InlineCode"]],
   "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"dd0f4627-3ba9-4246-841b-b7c40190e03d"],
 " says how to split the indices: the blocks must sum to the order of the \
array and each must be one, two or three, space holding no more at a time. \
The default uses ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"ArrayNesting", "[", 
    RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"f60f498c-fb8c-f548-b5f7-59ce4a3cf94e"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"e8df06a3-5e2f-fa45-acf7-fd61ce2837c4"],

Cell["\<\
The cubes have translucent faces and no outline, so that the entries behind \
them can still be read; an outline on every cube of a lattice reads as a mesh \
rather than as a set of cells.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"e82ae014-a651-5242-97d2-24ea0af16bf3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A gnomon in the near corner marks as many axes as the picture uses; ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"\"\<Gnomon\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "False"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"32186fff-fd22-ed4b-a06a-573b4e674f03"],
 " drops it. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"\"\<Indices\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<Colored\>\""}], 
   "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "decbddf7-39d7-5741-b250-a00b4827955b"],
 " gives each axis a colour of its own."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"c743a2cb-218f-1e4d-ad40-7e90ed35179f"],

Cell["\<\
The reference implementation this package grew out of drew only the \
order-three case, and called such a picture a cubix; the name is not kept, \
but the look of it is.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"6ee60acb-5896-8c4a-bf2a-9106ad07c0dc"],

Cell["The other options are shared with ArrayGraphics.", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"089833e2-4d59-bc4c-8d25-b04fc1cf6836"],

Cell["Examples", "PrimaryExamplesSection",ExpressionUUID->"da43b981-dc0c-0545-930b-f4c3fa5853c6"],

Cell["At order one a line of cubes, at order two a plane of them:", \
"ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"2ec3956f-ee87-2d41-92b1-9e463f2959f2"],

Cell["\<\
{ArrayGraphics3D[{1, 2, 3, 4}], ArrayGraphics3D[{{1, 2, 3}, {4, 5, 6}}]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"25be91c6-d523-cf4e-b82d-67563d2c4056"],

